# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scale Up — environment variables
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
#   1. Make a copy of it in this same folder.
#   2. Rename the copy to exactly:  .env.local
#   3. Fill in the three values below.
#   4. Save, then restart the app (stop it, then `npm run dev` again).
#
# .env.local is ignored by git, so your keys never leave your machine.
# Never share these values or paste them into a website, email or chat.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── 1. Anthropic — powers the AI drawing analysis ────────────
# Get it from https://console.anthropic.com  ->  API Keys  ->  Create Key
# Starts with "sk-ant-"
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=


# ── 2. Supabase — accounts and project storage ───────────────
# Full walkthrough in SUPABASE_SETUP.md
# Both values come from your Supabase dashboard:
#   Project Settings  ->  API
#
# The Project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijkl.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# The "anon" / "public" key — a long string starting with "eyJ".
# This one is DESIGNED to be visible in the browser, so it is safe here.
# The "service_role" key on that same page is NOT safe — never use it in
# this file and never share it with anyone.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEPLOYING TO VERCEL
# The file above only works on your own computer. For the live website you
# must add the SAME three variables in Vercel:
#   Your project  ->  Settings  ->  Environment Variables
# Add each name and value, then redeploy.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
